# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which is why
# every commit printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF". Without this file the first
# contributor on macOS or Linux gets a whole-file diff on any file they touch,
# for no reason anyone can see.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, and text is stored AND
# checked out as LF everywhere. Windows editors have handled LF for years; the
# few things that genuinely need CRLF are listed below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts that cmd.exe / the NSIS toolchain read line by line.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.nsh  text eol=crlf
*.nsi  text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
*.mov  binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.node binary
*.safetensors binary
*.gguf binary
*.onnx binary

# Generated — collapse in PR diffs so a lockfile bump does not bury a real change.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff

# GitHub language stats: this is a TypeScript app, not a docs/media project.
docs/**            linguist-documentation=true
examples/**        linguist-documentation=true
recipes/**         linguist-documentation=true
